## Migration Analysis

Your code has **three** patterns that break on .NET 8:

| API | Problem on .NET 8 |
|-----|-------------------|
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` (SYSLIB0006) |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Obsolete (SYSLIB0046 in .NET 9), unreliable for `WaitOne` wakeup |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` with no cancellation | Cannot be cooperatively cancelled |

Additionally, there's a **race condition**: multiple `Enqueue` calls between `WaitOne`/`Reset` lose signals, potentially leaving items unprocessed.

---

## Migrated Code (.NET 8)

```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;

public class EventProcessor : IDisposable
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();
    private Task? _processingTask;

    public void Start()
    {
        _processingTask = Task.Run(RunLoopAsync);
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(_cts.Token))
            {
                Handle(item);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            // Normal shutdown — cancellation requested
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        _channel.Writer.TryWrite(item);
    }

    public async Task StopAsync()
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete();          // Signal no more items
        _cts.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)); // Timeout fallback

        if (_processingTask is not null)
            await _processingTask;
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _cts.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item) { /* your logic */ }
}
```

